 "context": "These are the SNGPL lines that pick gas up from the big Sindh fields and carry it north. Unlike the Punjab distribution lines these ARE documented: Sawan (OMV, on stream 2003), Qadirpur (OGDCL) and Sui (PPL) all have well-reported development histories, and the Sui-Multan line (P4090) is one of the oldest and most-cited pipelines in Pakistan \u2014 the sweep already confirmed its existence off SNGPL's own province-wise transmission breakdown, so chase that same document for a date. P4101 'SV1-QV1' and P4079 'Sawan-Qadirpur' share both endpoints (Sawan -> Qadirpur) and may be the same physical line under a valve-station label vs a place label; if your sources say so, raise it as validity concern_type=duplicate rather than forcing two separate dates.",
